---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy and Cookies | ImmigrationPoints.com" description="Google Analytics audience measurement with cookies and no advertising, a cookieless Clarity stability check, calculator answers kept in your browser, and your rights.">
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-primary-dark text-white py-12">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-lg opacity-90">How we handle your data and protect your privacy.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose prose-lg">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mb-4">Our Commitment to Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      At ImmigrationPoints.com, we believe that access to immigration information should not come at the cost of your privacy. This privacy policy explains what data we collect (and do not collect) when you use our website and calculators.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Calculator Data</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      Our immigration points calculators run entirely in your web browser using client-side JavaScript. The personal information you enter into the calculators - including your age, education, language scores, work experience, and other factors - is processed locally on your device and is never transmitted to our servers. We do not collect, store, or have access to any data you enter into our calculators.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Audience Measurement with Google Analytics</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are useful: pages viewed, referring page, visit length, device and browser type, approximate country and city. To do so Google Analytics sets two cookies on your device: <code>_ga</code>, which tells visitors apart with a random identifier, and <code>_ga_43BP26Y79R</code>, which keeps the state of the visit. Their lifetime is set to 13 months at most (390 days) and is not extended on each visit; Google's default is 2 years.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      The IP address is anonymised: Google Analytics 4 neither logs nor stores it, and only uses it at collection time to derive an approximate country and city. The page address sent to Google Analytics is stripped of its parameters, and your calculator answers are never sent. The site shows no advertising: ad storage, ad user data, ad personalisation and Google signals are switched off, and measurement data is shared with no advertiser.
    </p>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      Purpose: audience measurement. Legal basis: the publisher's legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). Provider: Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, acting as processor under Article 28 GDPR. Data may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission's standard contractual clauses. Retention at Google: 14 months for visit-level and identifier-level data, then deletion; only anonymous totals remain. To object: block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary underline">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The site works the same way.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Stability Monitoring with Microsoft Clarity, Cookie-Free</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      No advertising network and no social media pixel run on the site. To check that the site works (errors, load times, clicks that do nothing), it uses Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode, in which Clarity sets no cookie, each page view gets a one-off identifier, visits are not linked together and page content is masked. The provider is Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited; data are kept 30 days (aggregates up to 13 months); the legal basis is our legitimate interest in a working site (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). You can object by blocking clarity.ms in your browser or by writing to us. Radif Partners, the publisher, records no personal data about the people who check their Express Entry or SkillSelect points here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      The site sets Google Analytics audience measurement cookies and those alone: no advertising cookie, no social media cookie.
    </p>
    <table class="text-neutral-700">
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Tell visitors apart with a random identifier</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_ga_43BP26Y79R</code></td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Keep the state of the current visit</td><td>13 months at most (390 days)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      These lifetimes are not extended on each visit. Microsoft Clarity sets none. The CRS and Australian points calculators keep nothing on your device: your age, degree, IELTS or CELPIP results and years of work experience exist only in the open browser tab and disappear when you close it. To object to these cookies, block or delete them in your browser settings or use the Google Analytics opt-out add-on described above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). Like any web server, GitHub automatically records technical request data in its logs, such as the IP address, date and time, page requested and browser type, to deliver the pages and protect the service against abuse. We do not use these logs to identify visitors; they are kept and handled by GitHub under its own privacy statement.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Email</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      If you write to <a href="mailto:contact@immigrationpoints.com" class="text-primary underline">contact@immigrationpoints.com</a>, we use your address and message only to reply, and delete the exchange once it no longer serves that purpose.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Data Sharing</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer any information to third parties. Access is limited to the host, Google Ireland Limited for Google Analytics and Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited for Clarity, acting as processors under Article 28 GDPR. Google Analytics and Clarity data may be transferred to Google LLC and Microsoft Corporation in the United States under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. Calculator answers are never collected, so they are never shared.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      Our website is not directed at children under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights regarding your personal data, including the right to access, correct, delete, or port your data, and the right to object to certain processing activities. Since we store no personal data from the calculators and hold no data that identifies you from your visit, there is usually nothing for us to retrieve; if you write to us, these rights apply to your email. To object to audience measurement without writing to us, block cookies in your browser or install the Google Analytics opt-out add-on. Depending on where you live, you may also complain to your data protection authority, for example the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada or the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date. Your continued use of the website after any changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
      If you have questions about this privacy policy or our data practices, write to <a href="mailto:contact@immigrationpoints.com" class="text-primary underline">contact@immigrationpoints.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mt-8">Last updated: October 2026</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
